{"title": "Quant Super Practice — Mock #150", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>For a certain article, if discount is 22% the profit is 17%. If the discount is 12%, then the profit is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; 22% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; 17% &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; 12% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["17%", "32%", "7%", "19%"], "options_hi": ["17%", "32%", "7%", "19%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let marked price of article = Rs.100</p><p>Selling price of article = 100 * 78/100 = Rs.78</p><p>Profit% = 17%</p><p>Cost price of article = 100 * 78/(100 + 17)</p><p>= 100 * 78/117 = 100 * 2/3 = Rs.200/3</p><p>If the discount is 12%, then selling price will be = 100 * 88/100 = Rs.88</p><p>Profit% = [88  -  (200/3)] * 100/(200/3) = 64 * 100/200 = 32%.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let marked price of article = Rs.100</p><p>Selling price of article = 100 * 78/100 = Rs.78</p><p>Profit% = 17%</p><p>Cost price of article = 100 * 78/(100 + 17)</p><p>= 100 * 78/117 = 100 * 2/3 = Rs.200/3</p><p>If the discount is 12%, then selling price will be = 100 * 88/100 = Rs.88</p><p>Profit% = [88  -  (200/3)] * 100/(200/3) = 64 * 100/200 = 32%.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A person bought an Air  -  conditioner at 15% discount on the marked price. If he had not got discount, he would have to pay Rs.2250 more. Find the cost price at which the person bought the Air  -  conditioner.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; 15% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2319;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2306;&#2337;&#2368;&#2358;&#2344;&#2352; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2352;&#2369;. 2250 &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2396;&#2340;&#2366;&#2404; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2306;&#2337;&#2368;&#2358;&#2344;&#2352; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 12750", "Rs. 13400", "Rs. 15000", "Rs. 11300"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 12750", "&#2352;&#2369;. 13400", "&#2352;&#2369;. 15000", "&#2352;&#2369;. 11300"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the marked price of the article be x</p><p>Then according to question,</p><p>x * 15/100 = Rs. 2250</p><p>x = Rs. 15000</p><p>Cost price of the article will be 15000  -  2250 = Rs.12750</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the marked price of the article be x</p><p>Then according to question,</p><p>x * 15/100 = Rs. 2250</p><p>x = Rs. 15000</p><p>Cost price of the article will be 15000  -  2250 = Rs.12750</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the profit percentage of a person on an article if the ratio of cost price and selling price of the article is 9 : 15(Approx.). </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9: 15 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340;(&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["48", "54", "25", "67"], "options_hi": ["48", "54", "25", "67"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost price and selling price of the article be 9x and 15x respectively</p><p>According to question,</p><p>Profit% = (S.P.  -  C.P.)/C.P. * 100</p><p>= (15x  -  9x)/9x * 100 </p><p>= 6x/9x * 100 = 66.66666 &#8773; 67%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost price and selling price of the article be 9x and 15x respectively</p><p>According to question,</p><p>Profit% = (S.P.  -  C.P.)/C.P. * 100</p><p>= (15x  -  9x)/9x * 100 </p><p>= 6x/9x * 100 = 66.66666 &#8773; 67%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The selling price of 15 oranges is the same as the cost price of 19 oranges. What is the approximate profit percentage?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>15 &#2360;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351;, 19 &#2360;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["15.34%", "18.75%", "32.5%", "26.67%"], "options_hi": ["15.34%", "18.75%", "32.5%", "26.67%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>Profit = cost price of (19-15) oranges = 4 oranges.</p><p>Profit percentage = (profit/cost price)  X 100 = (4/15)  X  100 = 26.67%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>Profit = cost price of (19-15) oranges = 4 oranges.</p><p>Profit percentage = (profit/cost price)  X 100 = (4/15)  X  100 = 26.67%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Rajkumar decides to sell his watch at a discount of 5%. However, his brother purchases it from him and receives an 8% discount. Rajkumar loses Rs.45 in profit as a result of this. What was the watch's marked price?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 5% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2351; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2361;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2325;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2366;&#2312; &#2313;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2361; &#2328;&#2396;&#2368; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 8% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2369;.45 &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.1500", "Rs.1410", "Rs.1430", "Rs.1560"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.1500", "&#2352;&#2369;.1410", "&#2352;&#2369;.1430", "&#2352;&#2369;.1560"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the marked price of watch = 100x</p><p>Price at which Rajkumar intended to sell the Watch = 95% of 100x = 95x</p><p>Price at which his brother purchases the watch = 92% of 100x = 92x</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>95x  -  92x = 45</p><p>x = 15</p><p>Marked price = 100x = &#8377;1500</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the marked price of watch = 100x</p><p>Price at which Rajkumar intended to sell the Watch = 95% of 100x = 95x</p><p>Price at which his brother purchases the watch = 92% of 100x = 92x</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>95x  -  92x = 45</p><p>x = 15</p><p>Marked price = 100x = &#8377;1500</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Riya sold an item to Vani at 10% loss and Vani sold it to Maya at Rs. 4950 at 10% profit. Riya bought the item by spending -</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2339;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 10% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2339;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2351;&#2361; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; 4950 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 10% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 7000", "Rs. 2000", "Rs. 5000", "Rs. 5300"], "options_hi": ["7000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "2000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "5000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "5300 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost price of item for Riya = m</p><p>Cost price of item for Riya = 0.9m</p><p>Cost price of item for Maya = 0.9m * 110/100 = 0.99m</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>0.99m = 4950</p><p>m = 4950/0.99</p><p>m = Rs. 5000</p><p><b>Alternate method-</b></p><p>Let the cost price of item for Riya = m</p><p>m * 0.9 * 1.1 = 4950</p><p>m = 4950/0.99 = Rs. 5000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost price of item for Riya = m</p><p>Cost price of item for Riya = 0.9m</p><p>Cost price of item for Maya = 0.9m * 110/100 = 0.99m</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>0.99m = 4950</p><p>m = 4950/0.99</p><p>m = Rs. 5000</p><p><b>Alternate method-</b></p><p>Let the cost price of item for Riya = m</p><p>m * 0.9 * 1.1 = 4950</p><p>m = 4950/0.99 = Rs. 5000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper purchased a car for Rs. 88500 and spent Rs. 1250 on transportation. If he sold the bike for Rs. 107700, then find the profit percent.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; 88500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2361;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; 1250 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; 107700 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["18%", "24%", "25%", "20%"], "options_hi": ["18%", "24%", "25%", "20%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>C.P = 88500 + 1250 = Rs. 89750</p><p>S.P = C.P * (100 + Profit)/100</p><p>107700 = 89750 * (100 + Profit)/100</p><p>100 + Profit% = 107700 * 100/89750</p><p>100 + Profit% = 120</p><p>Profit = 20%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>C.P = 88500 + 1250 = Rs. 89750</p><p>S.P = C.P * (100 + Profit)/100</p><p>107700 = 89750 * (100 + Profit)/100</p><p>100 + Profit% = 107700 * 100/89750</p><p>100 + Profit% = 120</p><p>Profit = 20%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper sold an article for Rs. 504 per article, there was a loss of 16%. If the shopkeeper incurs a total loss of Rs. 4128, then how many articles were sold?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; 504 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 16% &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 4128 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2305; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["37", "51", "47", "43"], "options_hi": ["37", "51", "47", "43"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>S.P = C.P * (100  -  Loss)/100</p><p>504 = C.P * (100  -  16)/100</p><p>C.P = 504 * 100/84 = Rs. 600</p><p>Loss = 600  -  504 = 96</p><p>Hence, the total articles sold = 4128/96 = 43</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>S.P = C.P * (100  -  Loss)/100</p><p>504 = C.P * (100  -  16)/100</p><p>C.P = 504 * 100/84 = Rs. 600</p><p>Loss = 600  -  504 = 96</p><p>Hence, the total articles sold = 4128/96 = 43</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A vendor gains 10% while buying the goods and 25% while selling them. Find the total gain percentage.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; 10% &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; 25% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["33.33%", "37.5%", "17.5%", "30%"], "options_hi": ["33.33%", "37.5%", "17.5%", "30%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>=&gt; For two consecutive gains x% and y%, net gain % age is given by</p><p>=&gt; (x+y+xy/100)%</p><p>=&gt; Here x= 10%,</p><p>=&gt; y= 25%</p><p>=&gt; Net gain = 10+25+10*25/100</p><p>= 37.5%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>=&gt; For two consecutive gains x% and y%, net gain % age is given by</p><p>=&gt; (x+y+xy/100)%</p><p>=&gt; Here x= 10%,</p><p>=&gt; y= 25%</p><p>=&gt; Net gain = 10+25+10*25/100</p><p>= 37.5%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>When Rahul sold an article for &#8377;1440, he earns a profit of 2R% and when he sold it for &#8377;1080, he incurs a loss of R%. Find the cost price of the article.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2332;&#2348; &#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369;&#2354; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#8377;1440 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 2R% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310; &#2324;&#2352; &#2332;&#2348; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#8377;1080 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; R% &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;&#2404; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Cannot be determined", "&#8377;1800", "&#8377;1200", "&#8377;1500"], "options_hi": ["&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;", "&#8377;1800", "&#8377;1200", "&#8377;1500"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let cost of article = P</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>2R/100 = [1440  -  P]/P ........ (1)</p><p>R/100 = [P  -  1080]/P ........ (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p>2 = (1440  -  P)/(P  -  1080)</p><p>2P  -  2160 = 1440  -  P</p><p>3P = 3600</p><p>P = 1200</p><p>Cost of the article = &#8377;1200</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let cost of article = P</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>2R/100 = [1440  -  P]/P ........ (1)</p><p>R/100 = [P  -  1080]/P ........ (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p>2 = (1440  -  P)/(P  -  1080)</p><p>2P  -  2160 = 1440  -  P</p><p>3P = 3600</p><p>P = 1200</p><p>Cost of the article = &#8377;1200</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A hotel is giving a discount of 12% on the booking of 2 or more rooms. Additionally, the hotel is offering a 5% discount only on payment using any cards of SBI. Rakesh booked 2 rooms in the hotel for a day at the rate of Rs. 1,500 per room per day.While checking out, he paid the bill using SBI Silver card. How much amount did he have to pay?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2379;&#2335;&#2354; 2 &#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2350;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2369;&#2325;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2346;&#2352; 12% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2335;&#2354; SBI &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; 5% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2375;&#2358; &#2344;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379;&#2335;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2352;&#2369;.1,500 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2350;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2366;&#2348; &#2360;&#2375; 2 &#2325;&#2350;&#2352;&#2375; &#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; (&#2330;&#2375;&#2325;-&#2310;&#2313;&#2335;) &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; SBI &#2360;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 2,498", "Rs. 1,254", "Rs. 2,508", "Rs. 2,618"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 2,498", "&#2352;&#2369;. 1,254", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2,508", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2,618"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Total amount of 2 rooms = 1500+1500 = 3000</p><p>Amount paid by Rakesh = 3000 * <img width=149 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image044.png\"> = Rs. 2508</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total amount of 2 rooms = 1500+1500 = 3000</p><p>Amount paid by Rakesh = 3000 * <img width=149 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image044.png\"> = Rs. 2508</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Marked price and cost price of an item are in the ratio 7: 4 respectively. After allowing a discount of 24% on the marked price of the item, item is sold at Rs.1330. Find the profit (in Rs.) earned on the item. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 7: 4 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; 24% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2352;&#2369;.1330 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; (&#2352;&#2369;. &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.130", "Rs.330", "Rs.80", "Rs.580"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.130", "&#2352;&#2369;.330", "&#2352;&#2369;.80", "&#2352;&#2369;.580"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Selling price of the item = Rs.1330 </p><p>Then, marked price of the item = 1330 * 100/(100  -  24) = Rs.1750</p><p>And cost price of the item = 1750 * 4/7 = Rs.1000</p><p>Therefore, profit earned = 1330  -  1000 = <b>Rs.330</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Selling price of the item = Rs.1330 </p><p>Then, marked price of the item = 1330 * 100/(100  -  24) = Rs.1750</p><p>And cost price of the item = 1750 * 4/7 = Rs.1000</p><p>Therefore, profit earned = 1330  -  1000 = <b>Rs.330</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Two similar pieces of an item were purchased by paying the same amount for each, and they were sold, respectively, for a profit of 25% and a loss of 20%. What was his profit percentage?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2368;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 25% &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2324;&#2352; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2354;&#2375;&#2344;&#2342;&#2375;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["2", "4.5", "2.5", "5"], "options_hi": ["2", "4.5", "2.5", "5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost price = p + p = 2p</p><p>Selling price = 1.25p + 0.8p = 2.05p</p><p>Profit percentage = [(2.05p  -  2p)/2p]*100 = 2.5%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost price = p + p = 2p</p><p>Selling price = 1.25p + 0.8p = 2.05p</p><p>Profit percentage = [(2.05p  -  2p)/2p]*100 = 2.5%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Sankar gives a note book free on purchased of thirteen note book and also, he offers 2% discount. Sankar marked at what percentage above the cost price of the note book so that he gains 40% profit on whole transactions?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2352; &#2340;&#2375;&#2352;&#2361; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335; &#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335; &#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2350;&#2369;&#2347;&#2381;&#2340; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2361;&#2368; &#2357;&#2361; 2% &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2349;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2375; &#2354;&#2375;&#2344;&#2342;&#2375;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; 40% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2344;&#2379;&#2335; &#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["53.84%", "61.89%", "45.29%", "38.72%"], "options_hi": ["53.84%", "61.89%", "45.29%", "38.72%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let marked price of 13 note book = Rs. 100x</p><p>SP of {(13 + 1) = } 14 articles = 100x * 98/100 = Rs. 98x</p><p>SP of each article = 98x/14 = Rs. 7x</p><p>Cost price of each article = 7x * 100/140 = Rs. 5x</p><p>So, cost price of 13 articles = Rs. 65x</p><p>So, marked up % = (100x  -  65x)/65x * 100 = 53.84%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let marked price of 13 note book = Rs. 100x</p><p>SP of {(13 + 1) = } 14 articles = 100x * 98/100 = Rs. 98x</p><p>SP of each article = 98x/14 = Rs. 7x</p><p>Cost price of each article = 7x * 100/140 = Rs. 5x</p><p>So, cost price of 13 articles = Rs. 65x</p><p>So, marked up % = (100x  -  65x)/65x * 100 = 53.84%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Three successive discounts of 20%, 25% and 5% given on the marked price of an item. What is equivalent discount % given on the item?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; 20%, 25% &#2324;&#2352; 5% &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312;&#2306;&#2404; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2360;&#2350;&#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; % &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["41%", "42%", "43%", "44%"], "options_hi": ["41%", "42%", "43%", "44%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Single equivalent discount for successive discount 20% and 25%</p><p>= 20 + 25  -  (20 * 25)/100</p><p>= 40%</p><p>And, single equivalent discount for 40% and 5%</p><p>= 40 + 5  -  (40 * 5)/100</p><p>= <b>43%</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Single equivalent discount for successive discount 20% and 25%</p><p>= 20 + 25  -  (20 * 25)/100</p><p>= 40%</p><p>And, single equivalent discount for 40% and 5%</p><p>= 40 + 5  -  (40 * 5)/100</p><p>= <b>43%</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Ankit bought a book at 15% discount and a copy at 10% discount on the respective marked price. If the selling price of book and copy for Ankit is Rs.680 and Rs.1080 respectively, then what is the total discount percent received by Ankit?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; 15% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;&#2348; &#2324;&#2352; 10% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2377;&#2346;&#2368; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;&#2348; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2377;&#2346;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 680 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 1080 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["16%", "15%", "18%", "12%"], "options_hi": ["16%", "15%", "18%", "12%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Marked price of book = 680 * (100/85) = Rs.800</p><p>Marked price of copy = 1080 * (100/90) = Rs.1200</p><p>Total marked price of book and copy together = 800 + 1200 = Rs.2000</p><p>Total selling price of book and copy together = 680 + 1080 = Rs.1760</p><p>Total discount amount = 2000  -  1760 = Rs.240</p><p>Required discount percent = (240/2000) * 100</p><p>= 12%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Marked price of book = 680 * (100/85) = Rs.800</p><p>Marked price of copy = 1080 * (100/90) = Rs.1200</p><p>Total marked price of book and copy together = 800 + 1200 = Rs.2000</p><p>Total selling price of book and copy together = 680 + 1080 = Rs.1760</p><p>Total discount amount = 2000  -  1760 = Rs.240</p><p>Required discount percent = (240/2000) * 100</p><p>= 12%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper sold 20 pens at 8% profit and 25 markers and 4% profit. If cost price of a pen is &#8377;10 less than the cost of a marker and the selling price of all the pens and markers is &#8377;1212, then find cost price of a marker.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; 20 &#2346;&#2375;&#2344; 8% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 25 &#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 4% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2375;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; &#8377;10 &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2346;&#2375;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#8377;1212 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;25", "&#8377;20", "&#8377;50", "&#8377;30"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;25", "&#8377;20", "&#8377;50", "&#8377;30"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost price of a marker = &#8377;'a'</p><p>Cost price of a pen = &#8377;'a  -  10'</p><p>Selling price of all the pens and markers = &#8377;1212</p><p>104% of 25a + 108% of 20(a - 10) = 1212</p><p>260a + 216a  -  2160 = 12120</p><p>a = 14280/476</p><p>a = 30</p><p>So, cost price of a marker = &#8377;30</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost price of a marker = &#8377;'a'</p><p>Cost price of a pen = &#8377;'a  -  10'</p><p>Selling price of all the pens and markers = &#8377;1212</p><p>104% of 25a + 108% of 20(a - 10) = 1212</p><p>260a + 216a  -  2160 = 12120</p><p>a = 14280/476</p><p>a = 30</p><p>So, cost price of a marker = &#8377;30</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>How much quantity (in kg) of red chilli powder costing Rs. 25 per kg must be mixed with 37.5 kg of turmeric powder of costing Rs. 75 per kg. So that on selling the mixture at Rs. 112.5 per kg, there is a gain of 80%?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>25 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; kg &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2354; &#2350;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2346;&#2366;&#2313;&#2337;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; (kg &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2379; 75 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; kg &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; 37.5 kg &#2361;&#2354;&#2381;&#2342;&#2368; &#2346;&#2366;&#2313;&#2337;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366; &#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2367; &#2311;&#2360; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; 112.5 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; kg &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; 80% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;?</p>", "options_en": ["35.5 kg", "22.5 kg", "12.5 kg", "17.5 kg"], "options_hi": ["35.5 kg", "22.5 kg", "12.5 kg", "17.5 kg"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let k kg of red chilli powder is added.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>(k * 25 + 37.5 * 75)/(k + 37.5) = 112.5 * 100/180</p><p>=&gt; 25k + 2812.5 = 62.5k + 2343.75</p><p>=&gt; 2812.5 - 2343.75 = 62.5k  -  25k</p><p>=&gt; 468.75 = 37.5k</p><p>=&gt; k = 468.75/37.5</p><p>=&gt; k = 12.5 kg</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let k kg of red chilli powder is added.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>(k * 25 + 37.5 * 75)/(k + 37.5) = 112.5 * 100/180</p><p>=&gt; 25k + 2812.5 = 62.5k + 2343.75</p><p>=&gt; 2812.5 - 2343.75 = 62.5k  -  25k</p><p>=&gt; 468.75 = 37.5k</p><p>=&gt; k = 468.75/37.5</p><p>=&gt; k = 12.5 kg</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Sharad sold 5 articles at 8% loss and 7 articles at 12% profit. If the selling price of all the articles is &#8377;6220, then find the cost price of an article.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2358;&#2352;&#2342; &#2344;&#2375; 5 &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2305; 8% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 7 &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2305; 12% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#8377;6220 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;420", "&#8377;700", "&#8377;680", "&#8377;500"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;420", "&#8377;700", "&#8377;680", "&#8377;500"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost price of an article = &#8377;t</p><p>Selling price = &#8377;6220</p><p>[(5 * 92/100) + (7 * 112/100)] of t = &#8377;6220</p><p>(460 + 784)t = 622000</p><p>1244t = 622000</p><p>t = &#8377;500</p><p>Hence, the cost price of an article = &#8377;500</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost price of an article = &#8377;t</p><p>Selling price = &#8377;6220</p><p>[(5 * 92/100) + (7 * 112/100)] of t = &#8377;6220</p><p>(460 + 784)t = 622000</p><p>1244t = 622000</p><p>t = &#8377;500</p><p>Hence, the cost price of an article = &#8377;500</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>An article is marked at Rs. 5500. Find the difference between selling price when discount of 40% given on marked price and two successive discount of 10% and 20% is given on marked price.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 5500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; 40% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 10% &#2324;&#2352; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 660", "Rs. 700", "Rs. 760", "Rs. 800"], "options_hi": ["660 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "700 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "760 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "800 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Selling price when 40% discount is given,</p><p>=&gt; 5500 * 60/100 = Rs. 3300</p><p>Selling price when two successive discount of 10% and 20% is given,</p><p>=&gt; 5500 * 90/100 * 80/100 = Rs. 3960</p><p>Required difference = Rs. (3960  -  3300) = Rs. 660</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Selling price when 40% discount is given,</p><p>=&gt; 5500 * 60/100 = Rs. 3300</p><p>Selling price when two successive discount of 10% and 20% is given,</p><p>=&gt; 5500 * 90/100 * 80/100 = Rs. 3960</p><p>Required difference = Rs. (3960  -  3300) = Rs. 660</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}]}